Z||000005||Monkeyman||07-12-2000||01:03 PM||||Kinda off topic (sorta).  I'll need to paint my new (in about a week or two) calipers.  What kind of paint will I need to use?  Anything labeled Hi-Temp?  Do I need Hi-Temp paint or will anything do?  I'd like to paint them a light purple, but I'm not sure I can find a color like that in a temperature resistant paint.  Suggestions???<P>------------------<BR>Dave-<BR>Grape Ape ('85GT)||||reg||1
Z||000006||87ECO5||07-12-2000||01:52 PM||||MM - not sure if you <I>HAVE</I> to use high temperature paint on the calipers (I am on mine) but here's a suggestion:<P>When painting my engine oil dipstick, I used Testor's yellow model paint - BUT - I surrounded it with high temperature paint.  In other words, I used HT primer, then the model paint, then HT clearcoat.  I've not had any problems with the model paint not holding up due to heat.<P>Just a suggestion ...<P>WOW!  It sounds like three of the IndiOhio members will have decorative calipers soon.  Too cool!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000007||87ECO5||07-12-2000||01:56 PM||||Darnit, Drew - I just reread your original post and realized you were asking what colors to use on your LCAs and UCAs - NOT your calipers!  DUH!  I'm such a dork!<P>Go high-gloss black on the L/UCAs, man, and use the same color on your springs that you use on your calipers!||||reg||1
Z||000008||fiero56||07-12-2000||08:14 PM||||I haven't decided on powder coating or painting yet. If I paint the calipers red, the control arms will be yellow, with red springs, and yellow spindles.<P>If I paint the calipers yellow, the control arms will be red, with yellow springs, and red spindles. <P>I plan to(hopefully)use a product from FoliaTec, which is based out in Germany.||||reg||1
